# Nura brand

Full spec: [`docs/brand.md`](docs/brand.md). Constants: [`lib/brand.ts`](lib/brand.ts). Logo: [`BrandLockup`](app/components/BrandLockup.tsx).

## Name

**Say and write Nura. URL is nurahelp.com (domain only).** Operator: **Receptly LLC** (`lib/legal-entity.ts`).

| Layer | Name | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Brand / chrome | Nura | Sidebar, headers, email from-name, Stripe Checkout, WebAuthn `rpName`, lockup |
| Legal operator | Receptly LLC | Terms, Privacy, footer copyright, JSON-LD `legalName` |
| Product feature | EMDR Support | Not the company name |
| Never in public | NuraHelp / NuraHelp AI | Domain host only — rewrite leftovers via `rewriteRetiredBrandCopy` |

```ts
// ❌ BAD
"NuraHelp"
"NuraHelp AI"
"Nura Help"

// ✅ GOOD
import { BRAND_SPOKEN } from "@/lib/brand";
import { legalEntityDisplayName } from "@/lib/legal-entity";
chromeBrandName(raw) // maps leftover "NuraHelp" → Nura
rewriteRetiredBrandCopy(text) // stored help/knowledge copy
```

Never lead with “AI” in titles, hero, or the wordmark. Do not invent a new logo — use `BrandLockup` with the wave wordmark (`tone="color" | "black" | "white"`; `href` defaults to `null`; wrap in `Link` or pass `href`). Admin lockup → `/admin`. Assets: `public/brand/nura-wave-logo*.png`, mark/favicon under `public/brand/` + `app/icon.svg`.

## Position

Calm guided therapy support — EMDR and resources in the app. Not an AI therapist, EHR, or emergency care. Marketing disclaimer: self-help, not a licensed therapist. No “find a therapist” / human matching — product is app-only.

Hero: **EMDR therapy online.** *in a calm app.* (tagline still: Support for therapy. Starting with EMDR.)

## Visual

- Pistachio palette: Paper/mint `#A4EDA5` · Sage `#84B067` (buttons, wordmark) · Ink `#2A3020` (body) · Pistachio `#C6D67E` **focus/hover only, never body or default field borders** · Olive `#948F4E` (muted) · Sidebar `#3D4129`
- Forbidden: OpenAI `#10a37f`, Apple `#007AFF`, Inter, purple wellness, hospital blue
- **Product type** (`/app`, `.app-shell`): **Source Sans 3 only** — remaps `--font-display` to sans (same idea as admin). No Fraunces in product chrome.
- **Admin type** (`/admin`, `.admin-shell`): **Source Sans 3 only** — sober UI; remaps `--font-display` to `--font-sans` so titles/KPIs are not ornamental Fraunces
- **Marketing type** (`.frontend-home`): Fraunces **only** for hero / major landing section titles + Source Sans 3 body + Roboto Mono kickers. **Legal / long-form public docs** (`/terms`, `/privacy`, …) use **Source Sans 3** for h1–h3 and body (weight 600 headings) — never Fraunces on “OUR SERVICES”-style contract headings. See **Frontend typography** below.
- Tokens live in `app/globals.css`. Marketing uses `.frontend-home`; product UI uses product tokens (see `product-ui` rule)

## Frontend typography (aligned with product)

Loaded via `next/font` in `app/layout.tsx`. Scoped on `.frontend-home` in `app/globals.css`.

| Role | Font | CSS var | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| Marketing hero / section titles | **Fraunces** (400; italic for emphasis) | `--font-display` on `.frontend-home` → `--font-fraunces` | Landing hero, pricing titles, editorial display — **not** legal docs |
| Legal + long-form public | **Source Sans 3** (headings 600) | `--font-sans` | `/terms`, `/privacy`, dense reading pages (override Fraunces) |
| Body / UI | **Source Sans 3** | `--font-sans` | Paragraphs, nav, buttons, intro lead |
| Labels / kickers | **Roboto Mono** (400) | `--font-alt` → `--font-fe-alt` | `.fe-eyebrow`, `.fe-section-kicker`, marquee — uppercase, ~0.9375rem |

**Rules:**
- Marketing hero/section titles: Fraunces weight **400**; legal headings: Source Sans **600**
- Heading/body **line-height 1.2** on marketing heroes; legal/long paragraphs ~1.5–1.6
- Kickers: mono, uppercase, muted color — never bold sans competing with the lockup
- Marketing and product share one voice; do **not** use Inter or soft rounded grotesks (retired: Libre Caslon Condensed, BDOGrotesk)
- Scale (desktop marketing): h1 ~4rem, h2 ~3rem, h3 ~2.5rem, body lead ~1.25rem, body sm ~1–1.1rem, xs ~0.9375rem (readable chrome floor ~12px). Legal page titles stay ~1.75rem / section ~1.125rem.

**Header (pill nav):** floating `frontend-header-pill` — logo | center nav **Home · How it works · Prices · Blog · FAQ** (hash links on `/`) | guests: **Sign in** + **Get started** pill; signed-in: name + avatar dropdown. No auth links in center nav. Styles: `frontend-header.css`.

## Copy

English, sentence case, short. No hype (“revolutionary”, “blockchain”, “neural networks”).

### Never say BLS to users

**BLS** (bilateral stimulation) is internal jargon. Do **not** put it in UI, emails, help, onboarding, billing, upgrade modals, status chips, marketing, or admin copy that users might see.

| Instead of | Write |
|---|---|
| BLS / free BLS / BLS minutes | **Free** / **Free mode** / **Free session time** |
| BLS running | **Set running** |
| BLS bar / BLS controls | **Controls bar** / **Session controls** |
| BLS preview | **Free session time** (or “live preview” for the gear sheet) |

Code/CSS identifiers may stay (`bls`, `TRIAL_BLS_SECONDS`, `.bls-dock`) — that is not user-facing. Extend `rewriteRetiredBrandCopy` if remapping stored help text.

### Visual sets — do not default to “moving ball”

Free / agent-guided sets are **not** “just a ball.” The product already has multiple stimulus options (e.g. Dot and Flash animations, stereo sound, gamepad rumble), and more will ship. Marketing and first-run copy must not collapse the product to one animation.

| Instead of (default) | Write |
|---|---|
| the moving ball / just the ball | **visual set** / **sets** / **session sets** |
| Free is the moving ball only | **Free is sets you run yourself** (no agent, no chat) |
| BLS controls → moving ball | **Session controls** (speed, animation, sound, repeats) |

OK to name the ball **once** on educational pages (`/emdr`, a guide about visual rhythm) as *one* way the set can look — not as the product definition, and not in Free headlines (“The moving ball, on your terms” is banned).

### Session modes (marketing + first-run copy)

Never use bare **“Choose Guided or Free”** on the homepage or other marketing — newcomers do not know what those words mean.

| Instead of | Write |
|---|---|
| Guided / Guided mode (alone) | **Agent-guided** / **agent-guided session** / **session agent** |
| Free mode (alone on marketing) | **Free session** / **Free (sets you run yourself)** |
| Choose Guided or Free | **Choose agent-guided or Free** — then one line: agent walks phases; Free is sets without an agent |

Product chrome can keep short labels (**Agent-guided session** · **Free session**) if the subtitle or card description explains the difference. Do **not** lead headlines with “AI”; prefer **session agent** / **agent-guided**. Internal code may stay `guided` / `free`.

Prefer **Guided** vs **Free** only in admin/internal tooling where the audience already knows the modes.

Public routes (must stay in `lib/public-paths.ts` + `app/robots.txt/route.ts` + `app/sitemap.ts`): `/` `/about` `/editorial` `/emdr` `/resources` `/blog` `/blog/[slug]` `/privacy` `/terms`. Also public: `/llms.txt`. Nav: **Home · How it works · Prices · Blog · FAQ** (hash links on `/` except **Blog** → `/blog`). Inner pages: breadcrumbs. Retired: `/therapy` and `/therapists` redirect to `/resources`.
